1. She is from the South of the UK. (Verbatim: "I can tell you I'm from the South.")
2. She struggled with pronouncing words containing 'r', such as "elephant" and "aerodynamics", indicating a regional accent. (Verbatim: "hyro, hyro, hyro, that was it, elephant.")
3. She grew up in a household with no alcohol, as her parents gave it up when she was born. (Verbatim: "Actually, they never had any alcohols at all in my house growing up. Like none, like absolutely none, because... my parents gave it up when I was born.")
4. She was very sheltered as a child and didn’t learn about alcohol or drugs until later in life. (Verbatim: "I didn't think I, I didn't, I don't know what alcohols were for like ways. Actually, so many things, so many things like I didn't learn until like too late.")
5. She was a very curious and inquisitive child, comparing herself to a raccoon exploring the house. (Verbatim: "I was very much like a raccoon, like going around the house with my little hands like 'I'mma go look for everything!'")
6. She had access to a wide variety of books at home, including a set similar to Encyclopedia Britannica, books on kings and queens of England, clouds, Chinese zodiacs, and fables. (Verbatim: "They had a book on the kings and queens of England. They had a book on clouds. They had a book on Chinese zodiacs.")
7. She always wanted juice boxes as a child but wasn’t allowed them because they were considered a waste of money. (Verbatim: "I always, always, always wanted these as a kid... I wasn't allowed them because apparently they're a waste of money.")
8. She has a poor memory for phone numbers and doesn’t answer calls from unknown numbers. (Verbatim: "I'm not very good with saving numbers, I'll be honest, I'm not very good with saving numbers.")
9. She would only answer phone calls from her parents or grandmother. (Verbatim: "the only phone calls I'd answer is probably if my nan called, if my mom called, or if my dad called.")
10. She compares herself to British kids who drank alcohol young, implying she did not, and disapproves of drinking. (Verbatim: "I wasn't as cool as the other British kids... Drinking is bad, alcohol is a poison.") [end of text]



1. She attended science summer camps during her youth. (Verbatim: "I did a lot of science summer camps yeah yeah yeah yeah yeah.")  
2. She participated in math competitions and math Olympiads as a child. (Verbatim: "I had to do a lot of math competitions... they did an Olympiad for physics.")  
3. She used to tutor young children in mathematics. (Verbatim: "I did a lot of like tutoring of like small small children okay like like mathematics.")  
4. She has experience with falconry, particularly working with owls. (Verbatim: "only a falconry on with certain birds though um mostly the owls the owls was the ones i worked on.")  
5. She struggled with being assertive during falconry training, which made it difficult to handle birds. (Verbatim: "i'm really really bad at falconry because i like the assertiveness in my voice... i'm just like yo owl come here and they'd be like no elliot you have to be like come here.")  
6. She prepared animal food by removing internal organs like yolk sacs from dead chicks. (Verbatim: "you have to remove the yolk sac because in oh actually i won't show you... you basically it's like squeezing toothpaste out of a tube but out of the butt.")  
7. She has a British accent and identifies as British. (Verbatim: "i can hear a British accent you hear correctly... i'm british okay.")  
8. She once accidentally broke the isolated heart of a guinea pig during a science experiment. (Verbatim: "I accidentally um accidentally broke a heart once and by broke a heart I mean a literal heart of a guinea pig... the heart was already separated from the body.")  
9. She is self-deprecating about her social life, stating she didn’t have friends as a child and still doesn’t. (Verbatim: "girl I ain't even got friends like oh sorry child I'm sorry I had to I had to give her the real answer.")  
10. She looks forward to going 3D so viewers can see her animated streaming poses. (Verbatim: "i am so excited for when i get 3d and you guys get to see all the dumb dumb poses that i do when i stream.") [end of text]



1. She previously worked with animals, including feeding live crickets to meerkats. (Verbatim: "we had like meerkats and we do a thing where we'd like let... the public would always be like heck yeah I want to feed the meerkats... I'd hand them the jar... of like crickets that are still alive")

2. She has experience handling jobs involving animal care that required confronting the reality of animals eating other animals. (Verbatim: "there'd be people... that were not ready and for some reason hadn't got it in their head that like animals eat other animals")

3. She has eaten crickets before, though in a bar setting where she didn’t taste them much. (Verbatim: "yeah i've had crickets but in a bar so i didn't really taste the crickets")

4. She is willing to eat bugs for content if her audience wants it. (Verbatim: "what bug would would you guys want me to eat bugs for content anything for you guys")

5. She admits to being a "simp" for cute VTuber girls and anime girls, calling it her weakness. (Verbatim: "cute vtuber girls are my weakness like they will always always i'm always weak to cute vtuber girls")

6. She describes herself as a fangirl who lurks on other streams and gets emotionally overwhelmed by cuteness. (Verbatim: "i'm a massive simp for for cute anime girls to be honest like i'm genuinely such a picking fangirl")

7. She experiences "cuteness aggression" and becomes extremely excited when encountering cute things. (Verbatim: "i have cuteness aggression i just get really really really hicking excited when i'm like i just i just can't cope")

8. She prefers her bacon crunchy, not chewy. (Verbatim: "do i prefer my bacon chewy or crunchy i prefer crunch tea yeah")

9. She has a habit of needing to "touch grass," implying awareness of over-streaming or needing breaks. (Verbatim: "Well, it's grass touching time guys!" and "I don't wanna but I must. The grass needs touching.")

10. She has limited success with Minesweeper, stating most of her wins are rare. (Verbatim: "The minesweeps that we've done today Are like the only time I've ever won At minesweeper") [end of text]



1. She strongly dislikes saying "bye-bye" and finds it unpleasant. (Verbatim: "It's not a bye-bye because I really, really don't like bye-bies. Bye-byes really, really, really, really, really, really suck. Bye-byes are bad.")
2. She prefers "see you later" over "goodbye" as a parting phrase. (Verbatim: "I would like to very selfishly request that it be a see you later if that's alright.")
3. She values viewer autonomy and does not want to force her presence on anyone. (Verbatim: "I can't force you, I'll never force anyone.")
4. Her goal is to make viewers happy and bring smiles to them. (Verbatim: "I'm here to try and make y'all happy... I'm here to try and make you guys smile.")
5. She acknowledges that she may not appeal to everyone, and that is acceptable. (Verbatim: "If I'm not to your liking or to your taste, then that's okay. That is okay.") [end of text]



1. She is originally from England. (Verbatim: "I'm 50,000 years old and I'm from England.")
2. She attended a university in England where she experienced extreme stress during her bachelor's degree. (Verbatim: "Probably during my bachelor's degree, when I was overworking myself and going through a lot of family stuff...")
3. She struggled with severe stress, low weight, and working multiple jobs while studying for her degree. (Verbatim: "I was also starving at the time and working three jobs and studying my butt off...")
4. She once made a university nurse cry when she disclosed her difficult situation during a health check. (Verbatim: "I made the nurse cry when I told her about my situation and I was so confused.")
5. She received urgent mental health support from her university's health center. (Verbatim: "She was like, over there you go, top priority, emergency priority, get her hacking in ASAP...")
6. She prioritized student care and happiness when choosing a university, not just prestige. (Verbatim: "Looking at things like, student happiness, student care, like, that is definitely, like, a really important thing, for sure...")
7. She has a self-deprecating humorous persona, claiming to be 50,000 years old due to stress. (Verbatim: "I'm 50,000 years old... stress is apparently the, one of the biggest aging factors.")
8. She jokes about using "copium" and "Delulu juice" as coping mechanisms for stress. (Verbatim: "My favorite anti-aging medicine, which is, it is what it is. Premium grade copium.")
9. She currently lives in England and comments on the weather, noting it's colder and has snowed slightly. (Verbatim: "I'm still in England. So it is English weather, and yeah, I'm surprised it's snowing...")
10. She expresses nostalgia for CRT monitors, recalling her family once owned one. (Verbatim: "And like, so my family had one of those.") [end of text]



1. She is a British VTuber. (Verbatim: "I'm Elias Alaria, British VTuber.")
