3. She has a strong desire to buy cute clothes now as a way to fulfill childhood wishes. (Verbatim: "that's a key reason as to why I like to get really, really cute, cute clothes, you know, I like to get and have things that I wanted when I was little but couldn't")

4. She has both British and Asian ancestry. (Verbatim: "my asian ancestors are very disappointed because i don't like spicy food" and "i come from a very working class british family on my british side")

5. She does not like spicy food, which contrasts with her Asian heritage. (Verbatim: "my asian ancestors are very disappointed because i don't like spicy food")

6. She associates her food preferences with her British working-class roots and describes her palate as similar to that of "middle age peasants." (Verbatim: "look i have the palette of my ancestors i assume they're probably middle age peasants i i come from a very working class british family")

7. She enjoys eating granola with yogurt and honey, and prefers traditional British foods like beans on toast, fish and chips, and biscuits. (Verbatim: "granola is delicious i have it with yogurt and um and honey" and "beans on toast beans on potato more beans extra beans bread fish and chips biscuits")

